## Step 1: Determine the number of potatoes the chef has left to cook.
The chef needs to cook 9 potatoes, and he has already cooked 7, so the number of potatoes left to cook is 9 - 7 = 2.

## Step 2: Calculate the time it will take to cook the remaining potatoes.
Each potato takes 3 minutes to cook. Since there are 2 potatoes left to cook, the total time required to cook the remaining potatoes is 2 * 3 = 6 minutes.

